---
description: >-
  Replays a short recording of raw records as an endless live feed. Every cycle
  moves all ISO timestamps to the current timeline and renews the identifiers
  that `demo::replay::renew_ids` selects. Expects the recording time in `time`
  and the record in `raw`, keeps other fields, and adds the number of the cycle
  in `replay.cycle`.
args:
  named:
    - name: max_events
      type: int
      default: 20000
      description: Fail for longer recordings, which would take too much memory.
    - name: speed
      type: float
      default: 1.0
      description: Multiplier on the replay rate.
    - name: start
      type: time
      default: null
      description: Start of the first cycle in the past, by default now. Records before now come at once.
    - name: cycles
      type: int
      default: null
      description: Number of cycles to replay. Endless by default.
---

demo::replay::internal::select_times raw
demo::replay::internal::timeline max_events=$max_events, speed=$speed, start=$start, cycles=$cycles
demo::replay::internal::render raw, shift=replay.shift, salt=replay.salt
